# OPTIONAL: Drupal test stack, for Functional and FunctionalJavascript tests
# run in the sidecar.
## Prompt: Drupal browser tests: lets the agent run Drupal's Functional and FunctionalJavascript tests in the sidecar, with a browser in the image.
## Question: Should the agent be able to run Drupal's browser tests?
#
## Needs: the PHP baseline above, the drush wrapper Dockerfile.base installs,
## and phpunit.xml and vendor/bin/phpunit at the project root.
##
## The firewall keeps the web container unreachable from the sidecar, so the
## site under test, the browser and its driver all run here, on loopback.
## `drupal-fjs` starts chromedriver on 9515 and `drush runserver` on 8888 for
## the run when nothing is listening there, runs phpunit with any arguments
## given, and stops the servers it started when phpunit ends, so no browser
## driver listens between test runs. Each server starts in a process group of
## its own, so stopping it also stops the browser and PHP workers it spawned.
##
## WebDriverTestBase uses the W3C WebDriver protocol, so FunctionalJavascript needs a
## driver rather than a browser library. Debian's chromium and chromium-driver
## are a matched pair on amd64 and arm64, verified by apt's signatures; the
## build asserts they share the major version chromedriver requires. The runner
## uses only the pair recorded in /etc/agent-container-kit.
